INT. NEONARENA GAMING TOURNAMENT - FINALS STAGE - DAY

Lights flash purple and green. A crowd of four thousand is screaming. Somewhere a commentator shouts about a "clutch play" and the huge screen above shows a frozen game of dragons, and under the stage a smoke machine is making too much smoke, and in the booth ZED the team captain, LIA the sniper, OMAR the coach and PRIYA the substitute are already sitting down in matching orange jerseys.

ZED
(adjusting headset, whispering to himself)
Okay okay okay we are fine

LIA
(to the group, loudly)
Everybody is hearing me? Mic check one two.

OMAR
(thumbs up, chewing a protein bar)
Loud and clear

PRIYA
(to Lia, pointing at her screen)
You have the wrong crosshair she told us yesterday

LIA
(not looking away from the screen)
She is not the coach. Omar is the coach

OMAR
(mouth full)
Thank you Lia

The crowd roars. Cold air from the vents. A drone camera hovers near the booth like a very expensive fly.

ZED
(to the whole team, hands shaking)
Strategy is simple. We go left. Always left.

PRIYA
(raising hand)
Left was how we lost the semi final

ZED
(ignoring her, muttering)
Left is good. Left is good.

OMAR
(to Zed, gently)
Maybe also some right

ZED
(snapping)
No right!

The announcer calls their team name. It is mispronounced. The audience laughs.

LIA
(to herself, quiet)
Please not the live stream. Please not my mother watching

PRIYA
(to Lia, leaning over)
Your mother is watching. She is in the third row with a sign

LIA
(horrified, covering her face)
She has a sign

OMAR
(to everyone, standing)
Okay listen. One game. Nobody dies. We are here for the free pizza anyway

ZED
(to Omar, hopeful)
Is there pizza?

OMAR
(pointing off)
There is always pizza

PRIYA
(softly, to no one)
Then I am already winning

The countdown begins. A big red three. Two.

LIA
(eyes narrowed, whispering)
Left.

ZED
(whispering back)
Left.

PRIYA
(under her breath)
Right.

One. A horn BLARES.
